{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ac1d653c2e7970af8","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QLiaJ4u64ZSGSV6aXJVMEP","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-b0TCSB/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-b0TCSB-translated-rust/0d767b69-ab62-4fa8-8e41-e4011018e1f5/tasks/ac1d653c2e7970af8.output","summary":"## Result: no divergences found. All 6 functions are behaviourally equivalent.\n\nI read all four files fully, checked every C statement against its Rust counterpart, disassembled the C `.so` to confirm the compiler's actual semantics, and ran a differential harness. Repository unmodified (all work in `$TMPDIR/diffharness`).\n\n### Statement-by-statement audit\n\nI built a 1:1 map of every C statement to a Rust line. There are **no C statements without a Rust counterpart and no extra Rust behaviour**:\n\n- `create_state` C 58→88, 60-63→90-93, 65-71→99-106 (all seven field writes present), 73→108-110, 75→112, 76→115, 78-82→117-121, 84→123-129, 87→131\n- `destroy_state` C 91-96→143-148\n- `process_buffer` C 100-103→160-163, 105-107→165-168, 109→170, 110→174, 112-114→176-178, 116→180, 117→181, 119→184, 120→185, 123→188\n- `update_flags` C 127-129→200-202, 131→207-208, 132-135→209-213, 137→215, 138-140→216-222\n- `confuse_types` C 144-148→234-238, 150→240, 152-153→242-243, 157-158→248-250, 162-163→254-255, 167-170→260-268, 174→274 (C has no `default`; Rust `_ => {}` leaves `result == 0`)\n- `confusion` C 178-181→291-294, 183→296, 185→298, 187-189→300-302, 191→304, 193→308, 194-195→309-310, 197-198→312-313, 200→315, 201→316, 203→318, 205→320, 207→322\n\n### Specific items verified\n\n1. **Macro-expanded format strings** — dumped `.rodata` of `c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so` and compared byte-for-byte against the 16 Rust constants (`src/lib.rs:54-72`). All identical, including the stringified argument text `state->flags.counter` (C:137), `memchr_found` (C:117), `param1`..`param4` (C:178-181), and every trailing `\\n`. Note gcc rewrote the three specifier-free `printf`s into `puts` (hence those literals sit in `.rodata` without the `\\n`); the emitted stdout bytes are identical to Rust's `printf`.\n2. **Integer conversions** — `objdump` confirms `cdqe` for `malloc(capacity)` (C:76) and `movsxd` for `snprintf`'s `n` (C:84), matching `capacity as isize as usize` (lib.rs:115, 125). `movsx` for `char`→`int` on `memchr`'s target (C:110 / lib.rs:174) and on `bytes[i]` for `%d` (C:167-170 / lib.rs:263-266). `%u` used only for `uint_val`; `%f` gets `cvtss2sd`/`as f64`. `'0' + (param3 % 10)` truncated via `mov BYTE PTR`/`as c_char`.\n3. **Shifts / bit-fields** — `sar eax,0x3` confirms arithmetic shift for `(param >> 3) & 0x7`. Bit-field layout confirmed from the actual masks gcc emits (`and 0x7`/`or 0x78` on byte 1, `mov WORD PTR [rax+2],0`), which is exactly `types.rs`'s `flag1@0, flag2@1, flag3@2, counter@3:5, mode@8:3, status@11:5, reserved@16:16`. `update_flags` read-modify-writes and preserves `status`/`reserved` in both.\n4. **Side-effect ordering** — `count++` before the `Operation:` print; counter incremented before the `Debug:` print; `printf` before `free(state)` in the buffer-alloc-failure path; `Final result:` before `destroy_state`. All match.\n5. **`(int)(float * 100)`** — gcc emits `mulss` + `cvttss2si` (verified at `0x1600`/`0x1604`); `src/ffi.rs:25` emulates the \"integer indefinite\" `INT_MIN` result that Rust's saturating `as` would get wrong. Logic is exact for `f32` (no representable `f32` lies strictly between `-2^31` and the next lower value whose truncation is in range).\n\n### Differential testing (evidence)\n\nBoth `.so`s `dlopen`ed `RTLD_LOCAL`, invoked only through the 6 exported symbols, comparing return value + byte-exact fd-level stdout + raw `PackedFlags` word / `TypeConfusion` word / `capacity` / buffer bytes:\n\n- Per-call harness: **64,167 comparisons, 0 divergences** — run against release Rust (both load orders) and debug Rust.\n- Batched harness: **~1.54M return/state values and ~57 MB of stdout compared, 0 byte differences** — dense `f32` sweep (all 256 exponents, boundary regions around `f*100 == ±2^31`, inf/NaN/signalling-NaN/subnormals), random `update_flags` raw-flags×param, random `create_state` (capacities 0-63 plus random 32-bit incl. negative/`INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`), random `process_buffer` content×all 256 targets, random+grid `confusion` incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`. Also run against debug Rust.\n- **Allocation-failure paths** (unreachable otherwise) covered via an `LD_PRELOAD` malloc interposer: first-`malloc` failure, buffer-`malloc` failure, and all-`malloc` failure — identical messages, identical `NULL`/`-1` returns, identical `free(state)` ordering.\n- Exported dynamic symbol sets are identical (exactly the 6 names, nothing extra from the Rust cdylib).\n\n**Non-vacuity check:** three mutant C libraries were built; the harnesses flagged `status = 15→14` and `bytes[1]→bytes[2]`. (The third, `(param>>3)` → `((unsigned)param>>3)`, was correctly reported as matching — it is genuinely equivalent because `& 0x7` only reads bits unaffected by shift signedness.)\n\nNo reachable Rust panic exists (all arithmetic uses `wrapping_*`, `%` divisors are constants 10/4, array indices are constant, shift amounts are compile-time constants < 32), which the fully-passing debug build confirms.","usage":{"total_tokens":96059,"tool_uses":28,"duration_ms":929396},"uuid":"57cfba73-3640-454c-b7fc-15ec435efd17","session_id":"0d767b69-ab62-4fa8-8e41-e4011018e1f5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QLiaJ4u64ZSGSV6aXJVMEP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Result: no divergences found. All 6 functions are behaviourally equivalent.\n\nI read all four files fully, checked every C statement against its Rust counterpart, disassembled the C `.so` to confirm the compiler's actual semantics, and ran a differential harness. Repository unmodified (all work in `$TMPDIR/diffharness`).\n\n### Statement-by-statement audit\n\nI built a 1:1 map of every C statement to a Rust line. There are **no C statements without a Rust counterpart and no extra Rust behaviour**:\n\n- `create_state` C 58→88, 60-63→90-93, 65-71→99-106 (all seven field writes present), 73→108-110, 75→112, 76→115, 78-82→117-121, 84→123-129, 87→131\n- `destroy_state` C 91-96→143-148\n- `process_buffer` C 100-103→160-163, 105-107→165-168, 109→170, 110→174, 112-114→176-178, 116→180, 117→181, 119→184, 120→185, 123→188\n- `update_flags` C 127-129→200-202, 131→207-208, 132-135→209-213, 137→215, 138-140→216-222\n- `confuse_types` C 144-148→234-238, 150→240, 152-153→242-243, 157-158→248-250, 162-163→254-255, 167-170→260-268, 174→274 (C has no `default`; Rust `_ => {}` leaves `result == 0`)\n- `confusion` C 178-181→291-294, 183→296, 185→298, 187-189→300-302, 191→304, 193→308, 194-195→309-310, 197-198→312-313, 200→315, 201→316, 203→318, 205→320, 207→322\n\n### Specific items verified\n\n1. **Macro-expanded format strings** — dumped `.rodata` of `c_src/build/libtranslated_rust.so` and compared byte-for-byte against the 16 Rust constants (`src/lib.rs:54-72`). All identical, including the stringified argument text `state->flags.counter` (C:137), `memchr_found` (C:117), `param1`..`param4` (C:178-181), and every trailing `\\n`. Note gcc rewrote the three specifier-free `printf`s into `puts` (hence those literals sit in `.rodata` without the `\\n`); the emitted stdout bytes are identical to Rust's `printf`.\n2. **Integer conversions** — `objdump` confirms `cdqe` for `malloc(capacity)` (C:76) and `movsxd` for `snprintf`'s `n` (C:84), matching `capacity as isize as usize` (lib.rs:115, 125). `movsx` for `char`→`int` on `memchr`'s target (C:110 / lib.rs:174) and on `bytes[i]` for `%d` (C:167-170 / lib.rs:263-266). `%u` used only for `uint_val`; `%f` gets `cvtss2sd`/`as f64`. `'0' + (param3 % 10)` truncated via `mov BYTE PTR`/`as c_char`.\n3. **Shifts / bit-fields** — `sar eax,0x3` confirms arithmetic shift for `(param >> 3) & 0x7`. Bit-field layout confirmed from the actual masks gcc emits (`and 0x7`/`or 0x78` on byte 1, `mov WORD PTR [rax+2],0`), which is exactly `types.rs`'s `flag1@0, flag2@1, flag3@2, counter@3:5, mode@8:3, status@11:5, reserved@16:16`. `update_flags` read-modify-writes and preserves `status`/`reserved` in both.\n4. **Side-effect ordering** — `count++` before the `Operation:` print; counter incremented before the `Debug:` print; `printf` before `free(state)` in the buffer-alloc-failure path; `Final result:` before `destroy_state`. All match.\n5. **`(int)(float * 100)`** — gcc emits `mulss` + `cvttss2si` (verified at `0x1600`/`0x1604`); `src/ffi.rs:25` emulates the \"integer indefinite\" `INT_MIN` result that Rust's saturating `as` would get wrong. Logic is exact for `f32` (no representable `f32` lies strictly between `-2^31` and the next lower value whose truncation is in range).\n\n### Differential testing (evidence)\n\nBoth `.so`s `dlopen`ed `RTLD_LOCAL`, invoked only through the 6 exported symbols, comparing return value + byte-exact fd-level stdout + raw `PackedFlags` word / `TypeConfusion` word / `capacity` / buffer bytes:\n\n- Per-call harness: **64,167 comparisons, 0 divergences** — run against release Rust (both load orders) and debug Rust.\n- Batched harness: **~1.54M return/state values and ~57 MB of stdout compared, 0 byte differences** — dense `f32` sweep (all 256 exponents, boundary regions around `f*100 == ±2^31`, inf/NaN/signalling-NaN/subnormals), random `update_flags` raw-flags×param, random `create_state` (capacities 0-63 plus random 32-bit incl. negative/`INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`), random `process_buffer` content×all 256 targets, random+grid `confusion` incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`. Also run against debug Rust.\n- **Allocation-failure paths** (unreachable otherwise) covered via an `LD_PRELOAD` malloc interposer: first-`malloc` failure, buffer-`malloc` failure, and all-`malloc` failure — identical messages, identical `NULL`/`-1` returns, identical `free(state)` ordering.\n- Exported dynamic symbol sets are identical (exactly the 6 names, nothing extra from the Rust cdylib).\n\n**Non-vacuity check:** three mutant C libraries were built; the harnesses flagged `status = 15→14` and `bytes[1]→bytes[2]`. (The third, `(param>>3)` → `((unsigned)param>>3)`, was correctly reported as matching — it is genuinely equivalent because `& 0x7` only reads bits unaffected by shift signedness.)\n\nNo reachable Rust panic exists (all arithmetic uses `wrapping_*`, `%` divisors are constants 10/4, array indices are constant, shift amounts are compile-time constants < 32), which the fully-passing debug build confirms."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac1d653c2e7970af8 (use SendMessage with to: 'ac1d653c2e7970af8', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 98213\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 929397</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d767b69-ab62-4fa8-8e41-e4011018e1f5","uuid":"933cf47e-3468-4dc1-b6eb-5f806a365128","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:28:13.916Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are hunting for behavioural divergences between a C library and its Rust translation. Do NOT modify any files in the repository. Report findings only.\n\nRepository: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-b0TCSB/translated_rust\n- C ground truth: c_src/src/lib.c (208 lines, 6 functions: create_state, destroy_state, process_buffer, update_flags, confuse_types, confusion)\n- Rust: s