{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ks47xj4vf37p73c5lhvak745b4u4e67uchszrjxd5gsmkjgynrqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Result: the Rust translation matches the C ground truth exactly — no divergences found\n\n### Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | All **6** C exports (`create_state`, `destroy_state`, `process_buffer`, `update_flags`, `confuse_types`, `confusion`). `nm -D` diff is **empty** — nothing missing, nothing needed translating. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **20** rows, one per distinct rejection branch mechanically grepped from `lib.c` (4× `state == NULL`, 2× `buffer == NULL`, both `malloc`-failure paths, `memchr` miss, `remaining == 0`, `switch` fall-through, the UB float→int cast, plus generic FFI boundaries). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **30** rows over the axes the C actually branches on (capacity sign/size, `snprintf` truncation points, all 256 target bytes, bit-field cross-products, counter wrap, 4 operations × payload classes, `%10`/`%4` sign behaviour). |\n\n**Feature combinations: exactly one.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options/`#ifdef`, so `--no-default-features` is the only combination. `cargo check` passes.\n\n### Phases B/C/D — all rows pass\n58 tests (30 valid-path, 21 error-path, 4 smoke, 3 symbol), green in **both debug and release** cdylib builds. Both `.so`s are `dlopen`ed with `libloading` and invoked *only* through exported symbols; every call compares return value, **byte-exact stdout** (fd-level capture), and the resulting `ProcessState` (raw `PackedFlags` word, raw union bits, `capacity`, buffer bytes).\n\n### Three real problems I found and fixed — in the harness, not the translation\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds a cdylib-only lib.** My first mutation run showed *zero* of 14 injected bugs being caught — the tests were loading a stale `.so`. Fixed with an explicit `cargo build` step plus an `assert_fresh` staleness guard that hard-fails if the `.so` is older than `src/*.rs`.\n2. **LLVM deletes a `malloc` whose result is only null-checked**, which silently turned the release-mode heap-exhaustion loop into a no-op. Fixed with `black_box`; the release OOM tests now genuinely prove the optimised Rust `create_state` still returns `NULL` and prints the same message.\n3. **Symbol interposition** would have made every comparison meaningless (both `.so`s export the same 6 names and C's `confusion` calls them via PLT). `RTLD_LOCAL` handles it; `tests/smoke.rs` proves it by comparing against a standalone C driver and checking load order doesn't matter.\n\n### Non-vacuity proven\n`./mutation_check.sh` injects 14 deliberate bugs and confirms **all 14 are caught** (wrong bit-field offset, mis-wired accessor, saturating vs `cvttss2si`, unsigned vs signed `char`, `%d` vs `%u`, wrong `snprintf` size, zero- vs sign-extended `capacity`, wrong sentinel, `switch` fall-through, off-by-ones). Two initially-uncaught mutations turned out to be *semantically equivalent* no-ops, not test gaps.\n\n### Independently corroborated\nTwo audit agents did statement-by-statement C↔Rust comparisons with `gcc -E` and `objdump`; both reported equivalence for all 6 functions. One exhaustively verified the `cvttss2si` emulation and the `f32→f64` `%f` promotion over **all 2³² bit patterns**. I confirmed gcc's `mulss`/`cvttss2si` codegen and the exact struct layout (`24/8`, offsets `0/4/8/16`, initial `PackedFlags` word `0x00007B05`) with my own `objdump` and `offsetof` probe.\n\nTwo sub-behavioural differences are documented in `VERIFICATION.md` rather than \"fixed\": gcc's `printf`→`puts` strength reduction (release Rust does the same; identical bytes) and internal PLT vs direct calls (only observable via `LD_PRELOAD` of those exact names). Nothing in `c_src/` was modified; the only `Cargo.toml` change is `libloading` in `[dev-dependencies]`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448,"cache_read_input_tokens":168167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":448,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d767b69-ab62-4fa8-8e41-e4011018e1f5","uuid":"34a4f26e-3cec-4960-9111-b0afd778132e","timestamp":"2026-08-19T19:29:21.026Z"}
